# ── RETIRED in 2.0 (do not re-add) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# engine.lua      DELETED — replaced by core_sched/core_timers/core_lifecycle/core_api.
# encounters.lua  DELETED — replaced by the declarative registry in core_api.lua.
#
# NOTHING IS PARKED ANY MORE. W4b was the last wave with a 1.x data file left on
# disk, and it consumed it.
#
# W4a CLOSES WAVE 4. Molten Core, Onyxia's Lair and the world bosses NEVER had 1.x
# data files — data_naxxramas / data_aq40 / data_bwl were the only three that ever
# existed — so there was nothing to diff, nothing to restore and nothing to retire on
# this side. With W4a in, no parked data file remains anywhere in the addon and the
# `Addon:RegisterRaid` refusal shim in core_boot.lua has outlived its last legacy
# caller class: every raid in the options tree is now PROJECTED from the encounter
# registry (core_api.lua §E).
#
# data_naxxramas.lua  DELETED in W4d — enc_naxxramas.lua replaces it. Its values
#   were diffed against the spec first; every disagreement is in the wave report and
#   the CHANGELOG, and the spec won each one.
# data_aq40.lua       DELETED in W4c — enc_aq40.lua replaces it, on the same terms.
#   AQ20 had no 1.x predecessor at all; enc_aq20.lua is new ground.
# data_bwl.lua        DELETED in W4b — enc_bwl.lua replaces it, on the same terms.
#   It was the last cross-check input; it was diffed row by row, the spec won every
#   disagreement, one log-verified mechanic the spec lacks was carried over
#   default-off (Vaelastrasz's Fire Nova), and a file that is both parked and
#   superseded is just a second source of truth waiting to be edited by mistake.
#   Zul'Gurub had no 1.x predecessor at all; enc_zg.lua is new ground.
